# Vegetable Pho with Crispy Tofu

Based on [Love and Lemons](https://www.loveandlemons.com/easy-vegetarian-pho) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251206153744/https://www.loveandlemons.com/easy-vegetarian-pho/)) and [The Viet Vegan](https://thevietvegan.com/homemade-vegan-vietnamese-pho) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251013162403/https://thevietvegan.com/homemade-vegan-vietnamese-pho/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For the Broth

- [ ] 8 oz [dried shiitake mushrooms]{ ing="dried-shiitake-mushrooms" }
- [ ] 2-3 medium [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, cut into 2-3 inch chunks
- [ ] 1/2 [daikon radish]{ ing="daikon-radish" }, peeled and cut into coins (or substitute regular radish, kohlrabi, or extra carrot) - [Jicama?]
- [ ] 1 [apple or pear]{ ing="apple-or-pear" }, cored and halved (adds natural sweetness, can substitute 1-2 tbsp sugar)
- [ ] 1 (4-inch) piece [kombu seaweed]{ ing="kombu-seaweed" } (optional, adds umami)
- [ ] 1 [white or yellow onion]{ ing="white-or-yellow-onion" }, quartered
- [ ] 1 (3-inch) [piece fresh ginger]{ ing="piece-fresh-ginger" }, halved lengthwise
- [ ] 4-5 [star anise]{ ing="star-anise" } (or 2 1/2 tsp ground star anise)
- [ ] 4 [whole cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" } (or 1/4 tsp ground cloves)
- [ ] 2 [cinnamon sticks]{ ing="cinnamon-sticks" } (or 1 1/2 tsp ground cinnamon)
- [ ] 1 tsp [coriander seeds]{ ing="coriander-seeds" } (or 2 tsp ground coriander)
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [fennel seeds]{ ing="fennel-seeds" } (or 1/2 tsp ground fennel)
- [ ] 10 cups [water]{ ing="water" }

- After simmering, add these seasonings:

  - [ ] 1/4 cup [tamari or soy sauce]{ ing="tamari-or-soy-sauce" }, plus more for serving
  - [ ] 2 tbsp [vegan fish sauce]{ ing="vegan-fish-sauce" } (or substitute 1 tbsp soy sauce + 1 tsp rice vinegar)
  - [ ] 1-2 tbsp [rock sugar]{ ing="rock-sugar" } or brown sugar
  - [ ] 1 tbsp [mushroom broth powder]{ ing="mushroom-broth-powder" } (optional, or use vegetable bouillon)

### For the Crispy Tofu

- [ ] 14 oz [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cubed
- [ ] 2 tbsp [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" }
- [ ] 2 tbsp [neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } (avocado, vegetable, or sesame)
- [ ] 1 tbsp [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } or tamari
- [ ] 1 tsp [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" } (optional, for spicy tofu)
- [ ] 1 tsp [maple syrup]{ ing="maple-syrup" } or sugar (helps with browning)

### For the Vegetables

- [ ] 2 [baby bok choy]{ ing="baby-bok-choy" }, quartered lengthwise (or substitute napa cabbage)
- [ ] 4 oz fresh [shiitake or oyster mushrooms]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" }, sliced
- [ ] 2 tsp [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }
- [ ] 1 tbsp [neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" }
- [ ] [Sea salt]{ ing="sea-salt" }

### For Serving

- [ ] 8 oz [rice noodles]{ ing="rice-noodles" } (bánh phở noodles, or substitute any rice noodles)
- [ ] 1 cup [mung bean sprouts]{ ing="mung-bean-sprouts" }
- [ ] 2 [jalapeño or Thai chilies]{ ing="jalape-o-or-thai-chilies" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1/2 cup fresh [Thai basil leaves]{ ing="thai-basil-leaves" } (or regular basil)
- [ ] 1/2 cup fresh [cilantro leaves and stems]{ ing="cilantro-leaves-and-stems" }
- [ ] 4 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 [limes]{ ing="limes" }, cut into wedges
- [ ] [Hoisin sauce]{ ing="hoisin-sauce" }
- [ ] [Sriracha or chili oil]{ ing="sriracha-or-chili-oil" }

## Recipe

### Prep (Broth and Tofu)

1. If using Tofuture, compress the [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } in the fridge for 2-4 hours
1. Wash and dry the [mushrooms]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" }, prep [carrot]{ ing="carrots" }, [onion]{ ing="white-or-yellow-onion" },

### Make the Broth

1. Preheat broiler and line a baking sheet with foil. Place [onion]{ ing="white-or-yellow-onion" } quarters and [ginger]{ ing="piece-fresh-ginger" } halves (cut-side up) on sheet. Broil for 10-15 minutes until charred and blackened. Alternatively, char directly over a gas flame or in a dry skillet.
1. While vegetables char, toast whole spices ([star anise]{ ing="star-anise" }, [cloves]{ ing="whole-cloves" }, [cinnamon sticks]{ ing="cinnamon-sticks" }, [coriander seeds]{ ing="coriander-seeds" }, [fennel seeds]{ ing="fennel-seeds" }) in a large stockpot over medium heat for 2-3 minutes until fragrant, shaking pan occasionally. If using ground spices, skip this step and add them in step 3.
1. Add [water]{ ing="water" }, charred [onion]{ ing="white-or-yellow-onion" } and [ginger]{ ing="piece-fresh-ginger" }, [dried shiitake mushrooms]{ ing="dried-shiitake-mushrooms" }, kombu (if using), [carrot]{ ing="carrots" }, daikon, [apple or pear]{ ing="apple-or-pear" }, and ground spices (if using) to the stockpot. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer uncovered for 1-2 hours. Remove apple/pear after 45 minutes to prevent it from dissolving.
1. Strain broth through a fine-mesh sieve into a large bowl, pressing on solids to extract all liquid. Reserve [dried shiitake mushrooms]{ ing="dried-shiitake-mushrooms" }, [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, and daikon if desired (slice and add to bowls when serving). Discard remaining solids (charred [onion]{ ing="white-or-yellow-onion" }, [ginger]{ ing="piece-fresh-ginger" }, spices, apple/[pear]{ ing="apple-or-pear" }). Return broth to pot.
1. Season broth with tamari, [vegan fish sauce]{ ing="vegan-fish-sauce" }, [sugar]{ ing="rock-sugar" }, and [mushroom]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" } [powder]{ ing="mushroom-broth-powder" } (if using). Taste and adjust seasoning - the broth should be aromatic, slightly sweet, and well-salted. Keep warm over low heat.

### Make the Crispy Tofu

1. Pat pressed [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes very dry with paper towels. Toss with [cornstarch]{ ing="cornstarch" } until evenly coated.
1. Heat [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Add [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } in a single layer (work in batches if needed). Cook undisturbed for 3-4 minutes until golden brown on bottom.
1. Flip [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } pieces and cook another 3-4 minutes until all sides are crispy and golden.
1. In a small bowl, whisk together [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }, [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" } (if using), and [maple syrup]{ ing="maple-syrup" }. Pour over crispy [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } and toss to coat. Cook 1 more minute until [sauce]{ ing="tamari-or-soy-sauce" } is absorbed. Transfer to a plate.

### Prepare the Vegetables

1. Heat [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } in the same skillet over high heat. Add sliced [mushrooms]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" } and a pinch of [salt]{ ing="sea-salt" }. Cook without stirring for 3-4 minutes until browned on one side, then toss and cook another 2 minutes.
1. Add [bok choy]{ ing="baby-bok-choy" } wedges to the skillet, nestling them between [mushrooms]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" }. Cook 1 minute, then add [rice vinegar]{ ing="rice-vinegar" }. Cover, reduce heat to medium, and cook 5-7 minutes until bok choy is tender. Add a splash of [water]{ ing="water" } if pan gets too dry.

### Cook Noodles and Assemble

1. Cook [rice noodles]{ ing="rice-noodles" } according to package directions (usually 5-7 minutes in boiling [water]{ ing="water" }). Drain and rinse with cold water to prevent sticking.
1. Divide [noodles]{ ing="rice-noodles" } among 4 deep bowls. Top each with crispy [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, sautéed [mushrooms]{ ing="shiitake-or-oyster-mushrooms" }, and [bok choy]{ ing="baby-bok-choy" }.
1. Ladle hot broth over each bowl (the broth should be very hot to warm the [noodles]{ ing="rice-noodles" }).
1. Top with [bean sprouts]{ ing="mung-bean-sprouts" }, jalapeño slices, Thai basil, cilantro, and [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }. Serve immediately with [lime]{ ing="limes" } wedges, [hoisin sauce]{ ing="hoisin-sauce" }, and [sriracha]{ ing="sriracha" } on the side.

## Notes

- **Spice substitutions**: If you can’t find whole spices, use ground spices but add them directly to the broth (not toasted) and strain them out at the end. Whole spices provide better flavor.
- **Kombu**: This seaweed adds deep umami flavor. Find it at Asian markets, health food stores, or online. Can omit if unavailable.
- **Daikon radish**: Look for this large white radish at Asian markets. Regular radishes, turnips, or kohlrabi work as substitutes.
- **Make ahead**: Broth can be made 3-5 days ahead and refrigerated, or frozen for up to 3 months. Reheat before serving.
- **Customization**: Add other vegetables like snap peas, sliced carrots, or cabbage. Some recipes add a cinnamon stick or cardamom pods for extra warmth.
- **Authentic touch**: For more authentic flavor, increase simmering time to 3-4 hours for a deeper, more complex broth.
